#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:1
msgid "Release 1.6 (2013-09-10)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:3
msgid ""
"In addition to the usual bug fixes, this release has several new features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:6
msgid "The command `nix-build --run-env` has been renamed to `nix-shell`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:8
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` now sources `$stdenv/setup` _inside_ the interactive shell, "
"rather than in a parent shell. This ensures that shell functions defined by "
"`stdenv` can be used in the interactive shell."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:12
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` has a new flag `--pure` to clear the environment, so you get an "
"environment that more closely corresponds to the “real” Nix build."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:16
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` now sets the shell prompt (`PS1`) to ensure that Nix shells are "
"distinguishable from your regular shells."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:19
msgid ""
"`nix-env` no longer requires a `*` argument to match all packages, so `nix-"
"env -qa` is equivalent to `nix-env                 -qa '*'`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:23
msgid ""
"`nix-env -i` has a new flag `--remove-all` (`-r`) to remove all previous "
"packages from the profile. This makes it easier to do declarative package "
"management similar to NixOS’s `environment.systemPackages`. For instance, if "
"you have a specification `my-packages.nix` like this:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:35
msgid "then after any change to this file, you can run:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:39
msgid "to update your profile to match the specification."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:41
msgid ""
"The ‘`with`’ language construct is now more lazy. It only evaluates its "
"argument if a variable might actually refer to an attribute in the argument. "
"For instance, this now works:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:45
msgid ""
"    let\n"
"      pkgs = with pkgs; { foo = \"old\"; bar = foo; } // overrides;\n"
"      overrides = { foo = \"new\"; };\n"
"    in pkgs.bar\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:50
msgid ""
"This evaluates to `\"new\"`, while previously it gave an “infinite "
"recursion” error."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:53
msgid ""
"Nix now has proper integer arithmetic operators. For instance, you can write "
"`x + y` instead of `builtins.add x y`, or `x <                 y` instead of "
"`builtins.lessThan x y`. The comparison operators also work on strings."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:58
msgid "On 64-bit systems, Nix integers are now 64 bits rather than 32 bits."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:60
msgid ""
"When using the Nix daemon, the `nix-daemon` worker process now runs on the "
"same CPU as the client, on systems that support setting CPU affinity. This "
"gives a significant speedup on some systems."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:64
msgid ""
"If a stack overflow occurs in the Nix evaluator, you now get a proper error "
"message (rather than “Segmentation fault”) on some systems."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:68
msgid ""
"In addition to directories, you can now bind-mount regular files in chroots "
"through the (now misnamed) option `build-chroot-dirs`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:71
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from Domen Kožar, Eelco Dolstra, Florian "
"Friesdorf, Gergely Risko, Ivan Kozik, Ludovic Courtès and Shea Levy."
msgstr ""
